#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:11
msgid "What I do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:13
msgid ""
"Stop the agent from hand-resolving merge conflicts in projected NEXT "
"files. These files are graph projections — total-rewrite from local state"
" every Stop hook. Conflict markers in them are noise to be regenerated, "
"not a diff to be merged thoughtfully."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:18
msgid "When `<<<<<<<` markers appear in any of:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:20
msgid "`.hero/NEXT.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:21
msgid "`.hero/next/<user>.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:22
msgid "`.hero/next/<user>.local.md`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:24
msgid ""
"run `hero next checkpoint` immediately. The command regenerates each file"
" from the local graph, discarding both sides of the conflict cleanly."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:28
msgid "Why this matters"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:30
msgid ""
"`hero next migrate-to-projection` flips `next.projected = true` and ships"
" a `hero-next` git merge driver registered in `.git/config` by `hero "
"install`. For clones that have run install, conflicts in these files "
"never produce markers — the driver regenerates the file on merge "
"automatically."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:36
msgid ""
"For clones that **haven't** run install (fresh checkouts, CI runners, "
"teammates picking up the repo for the first time), git falls back to the "
"default merge behavior and writes standard conflict markers. The next "
"Stop-hook firing of `hero next checkpoint` will catch it and regenerate, "
"but if an agent gets to the file first and tries to hand-resolve, the "
"result is wasted effort plus the very brittleness projection exists to "
"eliminate."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:44
msgid "What to do"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:46
msgid "**The instant you see `<<<<<<<` in one of those paths:**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:48
msgid "hero next checkpoint\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:52
msgid "That's it. Don't:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:54
msgid "Open the file and pick a side."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:55
msgid "Run `git checkout --ours` / `--theirs`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:56
msgid "Edit the markers out by hand."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:57
msgid "Try to merge the two halves into a \"best of both\" version."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:59
msgid ""
"The file's content isn't a source of truth — the graph is. Re-deriving "
"from the graph is faster, deterministic, and the correct semantic answer."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:63
msgid "Verifying"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:65
msgid "After `hero next checkpoint`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:67
msgid ""
"grep -l '<<<<<<<\\|=======\\|>>>>>>>' .hero/NEXT.md .hero/next/*.md "
"2>/dev/null\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:71
msgid ""
"Should print nothing. If markers remain, the projection failed (check the"
" command's stderr) — surface it, don't paper over."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:74
msgid "When this doesn't apply"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:76
msgid ""
"**Conflicts in `.hero/specs/*.md` or `.hero/planning/*.md`.** These are "
"hand-authored, not projected. Resolve them normally with the usual diff-"
"merge tools."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:79
msgid "**Conflicts in `.hero/knowledge/*.md`.** Same — hand-authored."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:80
msgid ""
"**Conflicts in `.hero/QUEUE.md`.** Projected, but covered by its own "
"regen path (`hero queue write`). The same principle applies but the "
"command differs."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:83
msgid ""
"**`next.projected = false`.** Pre-migration repos still use the hand-"
"authored NEXT.md flow. Normal merge resolution applies."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:86
msgid "See also"
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:88
msgid ""
"`skills/next-handoff-emit/SKILL.md` — the companion skill for *writing* "
"projection state during normal work."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:90
msgid ""
"`hero next migrate-to-projection` — one-shot to flip a repo into "
"projection mode and capture pre-existing NEXT.md content as graph nodes."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/skills/next-merge-recovery/SKILL.md:93
msgid ""
"`hero install` — registers the `hero-next` merge driver in `.git/config` "
"so future merges resolve without markers in the first place."
msgstr ""

